    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe [zip plugin](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/a373466cd984eeec7109c07c09e7d3d0978e5ff2/runtime/plugin/zipPlugin.vim) currently mixes archive command execution, `BufReadCmd`/`BufWriteCmd` integration, a browser buffer, member reads, member writes, extraction, and several security-sensitive compatibility paths.\n\nThis issue tracks the full zip plugin surface and related decisions to be tackled in a few PRs.\n\n## Existing behavior\n\nThe zip plugin provides the following functionality:\n\n- Detect zip-like files by extension and open them as archive listings.\n- Detect `zipfile://{archive}::{member}` buffers and read/write archive members.\n- Render a browser buffer showing archive members.\n- Open a selected member from the browser with `<CR>`.\n- Write changes from a member buffer back into the archive.\n- Extract the selected member to the current directory with `x`.\n- Support user-configurable zip/unzip/extract commands.\n- Fall back for non-zip files that match a zip-like extension.\n- Handle PowerShell fallback paths on Windows-like setups.\n- Preserve several path traversal, quoting, and remote archive compatibility behaviors.\n\n## Progress Tracker\n\n- [x] Add an opt-in `zip.lua` browser and member reader.\n\n  Enable it with `vim.g.nvim_zip_plugin = true`; while unset, `zipPlugin.vim` remains the default. The first implementation is private and read-only, uses `nvim.dir`, recognizes the complete zip extension set, and opens members through `zipfile://` buffers.\n\n- [x] Stabilize the minimum browser surface.\n\n  Settle extension dispatch, false-positive fallback, archive-directory navigation, syntax, member identity, and read-only buffer behavior before expanding the plugin.\n\n- [x] Add `:checkhealth nvim.zip`.\n\n  Report whether the required `unzip` executable is available and usable.\n\n- [x] Decide and port extraction.\n\n  Add an `x` action only after deciding the filesystem overwrite and path-handling behavior worth keeping.\n\n- [x] Decide and port member writeback.\n\n  Save changes from `zipfile://` buffers only after defining the update, staging, and buffer-state behavior.\n\n- [ ] Decide platform and remote behavior.\n\n  Treat PowerShell and remote archive support separately. The Lua plugin does not inherit the legacy `g:zip_*` configuration surface by default.\n\n- [x] Swap the default implementations.\n\n  Enable `zip.lua` by default once the selected surface is mature, and retain `zipPlugin.vim` as an explicitly loaded legacy package.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-08-04T08:46:34Z",
